<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baracoa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baracoa is a town on the north-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, founded in 1511 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez-de-cuellar">Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar</a> as the first Spanish settlement on the island. It served briefly as the colony's capital before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de Cuba replaced it. Isolated by mountains, it remained a small port for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baracoa.jpg" alt="Baracoa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Postiaux · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baracoa_-_El_Yunque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
